**Optional modernization** (unrelated to Thread.Abort migration):

If you'd like to modernize the parallelism style, you could replace the manual thread management with `Parallel.ForEach`:

```csharp
public void RunBatch(List<WorkItem> items)
{
    Parallel.ForEach(items, item =>
    {
        Thread.Sleep(100);
        item.Result = ComputeResult(item.Input);
    });
}
```

This is cleaner and uses the thread pool, but is **not required** — your existing code is fully compatible with .NET 8.
